Z||000001||Fierowrecker||09-29-2001||06:38 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierogtracer:<BR><B>Working on a system right now that uses Nitro like NOS. Any info on this magical liquid would be great..<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry to say, but that is the wrong aproach...<BR>Mix nitromethane with the gas, about 10% is safe with a stock motor...<BR>15 to 20% if it is built very well...<BR>I used to drag race, and used nitro occasionally, but it does not affect your performance as does NOS...<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||09-30-2001||07:07 AM||||Aack.<P>Warn me when you're going to be driving within 50 miles ;p)<P>Generally Nitro is added to the alchol before fueling of the car. I belive it does remain in solution and does not seperate out.<BR>Best!<BR>Ben<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierogtracer:<BR><B>Working on a system right now that uses Nitro like NOS. Any info on this magical liquid would be great..<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000003||falconhulk||10-01-2001||08:32 AM||||NOS is used to produce a heavy supply of oxygen quickly.  Thats what gives the engine the HP boost....well that and the extra fuel poured in to maintain mixture.  Nitromethane will not produce oxygen.  Sounds like a quick way to blow up an engine if you add it during engine operation in excessive amounts.||||reg||1
